Figure 2.5 ko aise parhiye, jaise ek pahari safar:
\(a\) (left end) par curve sab se neeche hai: absolute minimum, aur local minimum bhi;
\(c\) par curve apne aas paas ke sab points se ooncha hai: local maximum (ek chhoti pahari ki chotti), lekin sab se ooncha nahin;
\(e\) par aas paas ke sab points se neecha hai: local minimum (ek wadi);
\(d\) par sab se ooncha point hai: absolute maximum, aur local maximum bhi;
\(b\) (right end) par curve neeche utar kar khatam hota hai, is liye apne qareebi points se neecha hai: local minimum.
Andar wale points \(c\) aur \(e\) par tangent horizontal hai (yeh stationary points hain, 2.9.1).
